s8-6-p12 : Block
s8-6-p12 = prose (cons "The semantic classes must remain distinct. **Implementation-defined behavior** is selected by a documented implementation/profile parameter \(\theta\). **Unspecified behavior** is represented by the permitted choices in a transition relation, not by silently choosing one branch in a deterministic interpreter. **Undefined behavior** marks a violation for which the selected standard places no corresponding behavioral constraint on the program execution; it is not a distinguished, harmless return value. In a behavior-set semantics, a source execution classified as undefined may be represented by a top set of permitted observations, so a refinement theorem cannot rule out a target observation merely because the source reached that classification. Whether the semantics retains an observable prefix before undefined behavior is an *explicit choice of the formalization*: one cannot infer that the standard guarantees that prefix. For defined source executions, the target behavior must satisfy the ordinary observation refinement of §8.2." nil)
